Break a long number even when the line is already past the line length.
bc and dc insert a backslash and newline when the count of characters
on the line reaches one less than the line length, but the test was
for equality. A string printed earlier can move the count past that
point in one step, as bc's print "..." and bare strings do, and from
then on the test never matched again, so a number printed after a
string longer than the line length ran on unbroken for any length.
Break whenever the count has reached the limit.

---
 miscutils/bc.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/miscutils/bc.c
+++ b/miscutils/bc.c
@@ -5555,7 +5555,7 @@
 
 static void bc_num_printNewline(void)
 {
-	if (G.prog.nchars == G.prog.len - 1) {
+	if (G.prog.nchars >= G.prog.len - 1) {
 		bb_putchar('\\');
 		bb_putchar('\n');
 		G.prog.nchars = 0;
